# The box: Min width, Max width, Min height and Max height limit the size that the content or a percentage gives.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: The box · Minimum and maximum
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: demo
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 16 0
				Padding: 6 8
				Background: tint
				Border: 0 0 0 2
				Border color: accent
	Section:
		Text: The box
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Minimum and maximum
		Paragraph: A size between two limits is written with its minimum and its maximum. The maximum is applied first and then the minimum.
			Style: intro
		Text: Width: 30%, Min width: 200
			Style: label
		Text: 30% would be 154 points. The minimum makes it 200.
			Style: demo
			Box:
				Width: 30%
				Min width: 200
		Text: Max width: 260
			Style: label
		Paragraph: Without a width, this paragraph would take the whole line. Its maximum stops it at 260 points, and the text breaks to fit in them.
			Style: demo
			Box:
				Max width: 260
		Text: Min height: 70
			Style: label
		Text: One line of text in a box at least 70 points high.
			Style: demo
			Box:
				Min height: 70
		Text: Max height: 60, Overflow: shrink
			Style: label
		Paragraph: A box with a maximum height and more text than fits in it would be an error. With Overflow: shrink, its text gets smaller until it fits in the 60 points that the maximum leaves. The letters stop at the Min size of its Typography.
			Style: demo
			Box:
				Width: 260
				Max height: 60
				Overflow: shrink
			Typography:
				Line height: 120%
